---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base description="Saramsha Dotel — software engineer in New York.">
  <section class="hero">
    <img
      class="hero-photo"
      src="/assets/img/aboutimg.jpg"
      alt="Saramsha Dotel"
      width="104"
      height="104"
    />
    <div class="hero-text">
      <h1 class="hero-greeting">Hi, I'm Saramsha.</h1>
      <p class="hero-role">Applied AI Engineer in New York.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p>
    I am a senior software engineer on the Applied AI team at <a href="https://www.wbd.com">Warner Bros. Discovery</a>. Lately that's meant
    building search and retrieval over our roughly million hours of film
    and TV, and the evaluation tooling our teams use to compare models,
    prompts, and retrieval strategies.
  </p>

  <p>
    Before this I spent five years at <a href="https://www.naamche.com">Naamche</a>,
    a software studio I co-founded with friends in Kathmandu in 2020. We grew
    it from three engineers to forty and shipped real-estate, fintech, and
    agri-tech products for clients, mostly in the US. In December 2023 we were
    <a href="https://finance.yahoo.com/news/realpha-tech-corp-acquire-naamche-120000261.html">acquired</a>
    by <a href="https://www.realpha.com">reAlpha</a>, a Nasdaq-listed proptech
    company — the first time a Nepali software company had been acquired by a
    Nasdaq-listed one. I stayed at reAlpha as a tech lead for a few months
    before moving to WBD.
  </p>

  <p>
    Earlier I was a machine learning engineer at
    <a href="https://fusemachines.com/">Fusemachines</a>. I studied computer
    engineering at <a href="https://pcampus.edu.np/">Pulchowk Campus</a>,
    Tribhuvan University, in Nepal — I grew up there, and moved to New York
    for work.
  </p>

  <p>
    I read a lot and watch too much football. Mostly Liverpool.
  </p>
</Base>
